concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47A(6) Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-47a-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) The court hearing an appeal under this section: (a) must proceed by way of a hearing de novo, but may receive as evidence any record of evidence given, including any affidavit filed or exhibit received, in the court of summary jurisdiction; and  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia" ;
    skos:definition "(6) The court hearing an appeal under this section: (a) must proceed by way of a hearing de novo, but may receive as evidence any record of evidence given, including any affidavit filed or exhibit received, in the court of summary jurisdiction; and  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "80db1766a85767e70fb625680cfde364444055cc04d1d4764bfcc44cff3e04d3" ;
    values:partOf concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-47a ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must proceed by way of a hearing de novo." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
