concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-98 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "98 Section 69ZO"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-98 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the section, substitute: 69ZO  This Division also applies to proceedings in Chambers The following persons, when hearing child-related proceedings in Chambers, have all of the duties and powers that a court has under this Division: (a) in the case of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)—a Judge, the Chief Executive Officer, or a Senior Registrar or Registrar of the Court;  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 (b) in the case of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)—a Judge, the Chief Executive Officer, or a Senior Registrar or Registrar of the Court; (c) in any other case—a Judge, Registrar or magistrate. Note: An order made in Chambers has the same effect as an order made in open court." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the section, substitute: 69ZO  This Division also applies to proceedings in Chambers The following persons, when hearing child-related proceedings in Chambers, have all of the duties and powers that a court has under this Division: (a) in the case of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)—a Judge, the Chief Executive Officer, or a Senior Registrar or Registrar of the Court;  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 (b) in the case of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)—a Judge, the Chief Executive Officer, or a Senior Registrar or Registrar of the Court; (c) in any other case—a Judge, Registrar or magistrate. Note: An order made in Chambers has the same effect as an order made in open court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c9d30825db0b86e24b086d07adbcbaa3ba11d732b10601596c7ac368d8ebcdb8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Duties and powers for hearing child-related proceedings in Chambers" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2021a00013rec01.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.36" ;
