doc:sch-1-sec-200 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "200 Subparagraphs 18ZD(1)(b)(ii) to (iv)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subparagraphs, substitute: (ii) the administrative affairs of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); or (iii) the administrative affairs of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or (iv) the corporate services of the Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) and the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2), as referred to in subsection 18Z(1); and" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-201 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "201 Subsections 18ZD(2) and (3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-201 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute: (2) Before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome for the listed entity, if the outcome amount relates to the administrative affairs of a court mentioned in an item of the following table, the Chief Executive Officer must: (a) consult the person or persons mentioned in that item about the spending; and (b) obtain the consent of: (i) the person or persons mentioned in that item to the spending; or (ii) the Attorney-General to the spending.  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 Consultation about spending Item Court Persons to be consulted The Court The Chief Justice The Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) Both: (a) the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); and (b) the Chief Justice of the Court The Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) Both: (a) the Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); and (b) the Chief Justice of the Court" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute: (2) Before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome for the listed entity, if the outcome amount relates to the administrative affairs of a court mentioned in an item of the following table, the Chief Executive Officer must: (a) consult the person or persons mentioned in that item about the spending; and (b) obtain the consent of: (i) the person or persons mentioned in that item to the spending; or (ii) the Attorney-General to the spending.  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1 Amendments  Part 1 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 Consultation about spending Item Court Persons to be consulted The Court The Chief Justice The Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) Both: (a) the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); and (b) the Chief Justice of the Court The Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) Both: (a) the Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); and (b) the Chief Justice of the Court"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ed5785e2726446f0f6d63516e08fb4e17a6918bf0aae13845405fdc47419033b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consultation about spending before spending a part of the outcome amount for another outcome" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2021a00013rec01.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.54" ;
    cml:asserts concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-201-norm .
