concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-32ac-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32AC(8) Discretionary transfer of civil proceedings from the Federal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-32ac-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) The Court has jurisdiction in a matter that: (a) is the subject of a proceeding transferred to the Court under this section; and (b) is a matter in which the Court does not have jurisdiction apart from this subsection. To avoid doubt, the Court’s jurisdiction under this subsection is not subject to limits set by another provision." ;
    skos:definition "(8) The Court has jurisdiction in a matter that: (a) is the subject of a proceeding transferred to the Court under this section; and (b) is a matter in which the Court does not have jurisdiction apart from this subsection. To avoid doubt, the Court’s jurisdiction under this subsection is not subject to limits set by another provision."@en ;
