    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-236 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "236 Seals and stamps" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite the amendment of paragraph 123(1)(f) of the Family Law Act 1975 by this Schedule: (a) a seal of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of Court and in force immediately before the commencement day,  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia  Schedule 1 Application, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 may be affixed to documents (in accordance with subsection 59(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period beginning on the commencement day, as if it were a seal of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); and (b) a stamp of the Family Court, prescribed by the Rules of Court and in force immediately before the commencement day, may be affixed to documents (in accordance with subsection 60(3) of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021) until the end of the 12-month period beginning on the commencement day, as if it were a stamp of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "237 Continuity of Rules of Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-237 ;
    values:originalText "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this Schedule: (a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for the purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that are in force immediately before the commencement day; and (b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of those Rules of Court." ;
    skos:definition "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this Schedule: (a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for the purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that are in force immediately before the commencement day; and (b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of those Rules of Court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2a22dd1032457caf094a3ed855bf67911fd8e1edb0484a966680bc5546d33c7c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Amendments do not affect continuity of certain Rules of Court." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2021a00013rec01.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.67" ;
    cml:asserts concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237-norm .
concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237-norm a values:Undertaking ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-237 ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-237 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "237 Continuity of Rules of Court" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The amendments made by items 130, 139, 152, 165 and 167 of this Schedule: (a) do not affect the continuity of any Rules of Court made for the purposes of section 123 of the Family Law Act 1975 that are in force immediately before the commencement day; and (b) to avoid doubt, do not prevent the amendment or repeal of those Rules of Court." ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-1-sec-238 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "238 Registries of the Federal Court of Australia"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-238 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Despite the amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 by this Schedule, a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia, existing immediately before the commencement day, continues in existence on and after that day. (2) The amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 by this Schedule does not affect: (a) the designation, before the commencement day, of a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia as the Principal Registry of the Court; or  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Despite the amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 by this Schedule, a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia, existing immediately before the commencement day, continues in existence on and after that day. (2) The amendment of section 34 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 by this Schedule does not affect: (a) the designation, before the commencement day, of a Registry of the Federal Court of Australia as the Principal Registry of the Court; or  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e1a28c9a400f327c48c354a45ca0aa520a44eb95d925fe9c5d27eee39e7bffe6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "67"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continuation of existing Registry on commencement day" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2021a00013rec01.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2021a00013rec01.pdf, p.67" ;
