concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-56 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56 Paragraph (zf) of Schedule 1"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-56 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the paragraph, substitute:  Schedule 2  Further consequential amendments  Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 No. 13, 2021 (zf) the following decisions under the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021: (i) decisions of the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) or the Minister whether to consent as mentioned in paragraph 12(1)(a) of that Act; (ii) decisions of the Chief Justice or Deputy Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) in the exercise of, or in assisting in the exercise of, the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 47(2) of that Act; (iii) decisions of the Chief Judge or a Deputy Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in the exercise of, or in assisting in the exercise of, the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 144(2) of that Act; (iv) decisions of the Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in the exercise of the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 147(1) of that Act. Admiralty Act 1988" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the paragraph, substitute:  Schedule 2  Further consequential amendments  Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 No. 13, 2021 (zf) the following decisions under the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021: (i) decisions of the Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) or the Minister whether to consent as mentioned in paragraph 12(1)(a) of that Act; (ii) decisions of the Chief Justice or Deputy Chief Justice of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) in the exercise of, or in assisting in the exercise of, the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 47(2) of that Act; (iii) decisions of the Chief Judge or a Deputy Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in the exercise of, or in assisting in the exercise of, the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 144(2) of that Act; (iv) decisions of the Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in the exercise of the functions or powers mentioned in subsection 147(1) of that Act. Admiralty Act 1988"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d5a6133f4646c33f3272700537a87623f3037ddb31d87e4b41b1dfe830e912e6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer ;
