concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-106-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "106 Appeals from courts of summary jurisdiction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-106-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Family Court of a State has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary jurisdiction of the State. Note: See sections 47A and 47B of the Family Law Act 1975. (2) The Supreme Court of the Northern Territory has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary jurisdiction of the Northern Territory. Note: See sections 47A and 47B of the Family Law Act 1975." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A Family Court of a State has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary jurisdiction of the State. Note: See sections 47A and 47B of the Family Law Act 1975. (2) The Supreme Court of the Northern Territory has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a decree of a court of summary jurisdiction of the Northern Territory. Note: See sections 47A and 47B of the Family Law Act 1975."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "468d65aca88df61533ce4f929f3ed1e07f5486c7f4164d761e87d5bf5261f4c2" ;
