concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-2-sec-676 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "676 Section 208 (table)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-676 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the table, substitute:  Further consequential amendments  Schedule 2  No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 Cross-jurisdictional appeals Item Unless expressly provided by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, an appeal with respect to a PPS matter does not lie from a decision of ... to any of the following courts: the Federal Court (a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) a court of a State; (d) a court of a Territory. the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) a court of a State; (d) a court of a Territory. the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) (a) a court of a State; (b) a court of a Territory. a court of a State (other than a State Family Court) (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (c) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (d) a court of another State; (e) a court of a Territory; (f) a State Family Court of the same State. a court of the Australian Capital Territory (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (c) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (d) a court of a State; (e) a court of another Territory. a court of the Northern Territory (a) the Federal Court;  Schedule 2  Further consequential amendments  Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 No. 13, 2021 Cross-jurisdictional appeals Item Unless expressly provided by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, an appeal with respect to a PPS matter does not lie from a decision of ... to any of the following courts: (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (c) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (d) a court of a State; (e) a court of another Territory. a court of an external Territory (a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (b) Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) a court of a State; (d) a court of another Territory (whether internal or external). a State Family Court (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) the Supreme Court of the same State; (d) a court of another State; (e) a court of a Territory." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the table, substitute:  Further consequential amendments  Schedule 2  No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 Cross-jurisdictional appeals Item Unless expressly provided by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, an appeal with respect to a PPS matter does not lie from a decision of ... to any of the following courts: the Federal Court (a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) a court of a State; (d) a court of a Territory. the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (c) a court of a State; (d) a court of a Territory. the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) (a) a court of a State; (b) a court of a Territory. a court of a State (other than a State Family Court) (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (c) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (d) a court of another State; (e) a court of a Territory; (f) a State Family Court of the same State. a court of the Australian Capital Territory (a) the Federal Court; (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1); (c) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); (d) a court of a State; (e) a court of another Territory. a court of the Northern Territory (a) the Federal Court;  Schedule 2  Further consequential amendments  Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 No. 13, 2021 Cross-jurisdictional appeals Item Unless expressly provided by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, an appeal with respect to a PPS matter does not lie from a decision of ... to any of the following courts: (b) the Federal Circuit and F"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "512fd7439771398c7c326c1a8bc4950222dc7f0c1218b33320fecf89ea0051e5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Appeals with respect to PPS matters do not lie from certain courts." ;
