doc:sch-3-sec-11 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "11 Certification of retired disabled Judges" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A certification by the Minister under paragraph 9A(2)(a) of Schedule 1 to the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999 before the commencement day that a person is a retired disabled Judge has effect, on and after that day, as if it were a certification by the Minister under section 122 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021 that the person is a retired disabled Judge." ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-3-sec-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 Right of appeal to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-12 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of: (a) a refusal, before the commencement day, of the Minister to certify that a Judge is a retired disabled Judge under subclause 9A(2) of Schedule 1 to that Act; or (b) a refusal, before the commencement day, by the Minister under paragraph 9D(9)(b) of Schedule 1 to that Act to give a direction; if, on the commencement day, the time for making an application for review of the refusal has not ended. (2) Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of any of the following decisions:  Schedule 3  Repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of: (a) a refusal, before the commencement day, of the Minister to certify that a Judge is a retired disabled Judge under subclause 9A(2) of Schedule 1 to that Act; or (b) a refusal, before the commencement day, by the Minister under paragraph 9D(9)(b) of Schedule 1 to that Act to give a direction; if, on the commencement day, the time for making an application for review of the refusal has not ended. (2) Despite the repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of any of the following decisions:  Schedule 3  Repeal of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "10106d8f253f7fccb2bdc0ae3469d98a274af1097f55cfb929e51dab6d192ac1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer ;
