doc:sch-5-sec-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7 Things done by the Family Court of Australia or Judges of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the Court To avoid doubt, the amendments made by this Act do not affect the validity of anything done, before the commencement day, by or in relation to: (a) the Family Court of Australia; or (b) a Full Court of the Family Court of Australia; or (c) the Chief Justice, the Deputy Chief Justice, a Senior Judge or a Judge of the Family Court of Australia; or  Schedule 5  Transitional provisions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "217"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-8 ;
    values:originalText "Officer (1) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) The Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia. (3) To avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument. (4) A determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "Officer (1) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) The Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia. (3) To avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument. (4) A determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7ac7fd3628436d7a533fbf0b14f89edfc43a29ed3fcba30cbe53c669dbafc783" ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia are taken to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
