doc:sch-5-sec-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "8 Things done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Officer (1) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) The Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Chief Executive Officer of the Family Court of Australia. (3) To avoid doubt, doing a thing includes making an instrument. (4) A determination under subitem (2) is not a legislative instrument." ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 Things done by, or in relation to, a Registrar or Deputy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-9 ;
    values:originalText "Registrar (1) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) The Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court of Australia. (3) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Deputy Registrar of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).  Transitional provisions  Schedule 5 Continuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court" ;
    skos:definition "Registrar (1) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, a Senior Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) The Minister may, in writing, determine that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Family Court of Australia. (3) If a thing was done by, or in relation to, a Deputy Registrar of the Family Court of Australia, then the thing is taken, for the purposes of the operation of any law on and after the commencement day, to have been done by, or in relation to, a Registrar of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1).  Transitional provisions  Schedule 5 Continuity of the Family Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9260d65bdba19f858cb7ef49de8d8c70242477956029eac3ea889f4432e7e16f" ;
