    cml:modality cml:LTL ;
    cml:operator "AND" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Chief Justice must deal with complaint if complaint made on or after commencement day and circumstances gave rise to complaint occurred before commencement day." ;
    cml:premiseText "Complaint made on or after commencement day." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Chief Justice deals with complaint." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::temporal_ltl" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-13 cml:asserts concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-13-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-13-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "MAY" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Chief Justice may deal with complaint if circumstances gave rise to complaint occurred before commencement day." ;
    cml:premiseText "Complaint made on or after commencement day." ;
    cml:conclusionText "Chief Justice may deal with complaint." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-5-sec-13 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13 Complaints" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If, in relation to a Judge of the Family Court of Australia: (a) a complaint is made, on or after the commencement day, about the Judge; and (b) the circumstances that gave rise to the complaint occurred before the commencement day; then: (c) the Chief Justice may deal with the complaint under section 48 of the new law; and (d) for the purposes of dealing with the complaint, the reference to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) in subparagraph (b)(ii) of the definition of relevant belief in subsection 48(4) of the new law is taken to include a reference to the Family Court of Australia.  Transitional provisions  Schedule 5 Continuity of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, and Judges and personnel of the Court  Part 3 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021" ;
    cof:pageNumber "220"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-14 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14 Change in title of judicial offices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-14 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The office of Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under the old law is the same office as the office of Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under the new law. (2) The office of Judge (other than Chief Judge) of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under the old law is the same office as the office of Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under the new law. (3) In this item: old law means the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, as in force immediately before the commencement day." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The office of Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under the old law is the same office as the office of Chief Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under the new law. (2) The office of Judge (other than Chief Judge) of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under the old law is the same office as the office of Judge of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under the new law. (3) In this item: old law means the Federal Circuit Court of Australia Act 1999, as in force immediately before the commencement day."@en ;
