concept:c2021a00013rec01-sch-5-sec-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26 Appeals to Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-26 ;
    values:originalText "(Division 1) (1) If: (a) on the day before the commencement day, either: (i) an appeal could be instituted under Part X of the Family Law Act 1975; or (ii) an application for leave to appeal could be made under section 94AA of that Act; and (b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act, on the commencement day the time for instituting the appeal or making the application has not ended; then, on or after the commencement day, the appeal or application may be made to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) For the purposes of subitem (1), an appeal or application for leave to appeal must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court made under Chapter 3 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.  Transitional provisions  Schedule 5 Transitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 (3) To avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) is to hear and determine the appeal or application according to: (a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021; and (b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and (c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant." ;
    skos:definition "(Division 1) (1) If: (a) on the day before the commencement day, either: (i) an appeal could be instituted under Part X of the Family Law Act 1975; or (ii) an application for leave to appeal could be made under section 94AA of that Act; and (b) despite the amendments to the Family Law Act 1975 made by this Act, on the commencement day the time for instituting the appeal or making the application has not ended; then, on or after the commencement day, the appeal or application may be made to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1). (2) For the purposes of subitem (1), an appeal or application for leave to appeal must be made in accordance with the Rules of Court made under Chapter 3 of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021.  Transitional provisions  Schedule 5 Transitional arrangements for appeals  Part 4 No. 13, 2021 Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2021 (3) To avoid doubt, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1) is to hear and determine the appeal or application according to: (a) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia Act 2021; and (b) the Family Law Act 1975, as amended by this Act; and (c) any other law of the Commonwealth, as relevant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c0eccef941b217f24c438bffeedf1d523ed3575153aebb7886e057c9be5240d7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "226"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Appeals can be made to Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia after commencement day." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
